._*
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research data and results stay local; the repository publishes the
# architecture, not the findings.
#
# The repo exists so others can read, clone and re-run the *system*: the
# runtime, the skill manifests and their implementations, the registry and its
# lockfiles, the benchmark harness, the CI. It does not carry the benchmark
# cases or their gold answers, the Arena's leaderboard data, or run traces.
#
# Two reasons. The paper is not on arXiv yet, and publishing the results first
# would pre-empt it. And a public gold answer contaminates the benchmark for
# everyone who clones it — the hidden split only means something if it stays
# hidden.
#
# Framework code, schemas and data cards under these directories are NOT
# ignored and should be committed; only data and results are.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BioScience-Harness/benchmarks/cases/**
BioScience-Harness/benchmarks/hidden/**
!BioScience-Harness/benchmarks/cases/README.md
!BioScience-Harness/benchmarks/hidden/README.md
arena/web/data/*.json
arena/web/runs/*
!arena/web/runs/.gitkeep
# The example set is committed on purpose: the site must be demonstrable on a
# fresh clone, where the generated files above do not exist. It carries
# placeholder rows only — no real scores, no run traces.
!arena/web/data/*.example.json

# Paper source and PDF. These live outside this working tree by design (in
# `TCM+AI/paper/`), so nothing should ever appear here; the rule is a backstop.
paper/
plan/
